course: dictionary
lesson: 4389
title: Writing a haiku
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A haiku is a very short poem from Japan, usually with three lines. The clues are in the numbers: «In English schools a haiku is usually three lines of 5, 7 and 5 syllables.» A syllable is one beat in a word: "sun" has 1, and "blos-som" has 2.
explain: Haiku often catch one small moment, usually about nature or a season. «Haiku are often about nature, but they can catch any small everyday moment, even at a petrol station.» So a haiku does not have to be about a forest. A busy petrol station can be the subject too.
explain: To check your count, clap the beats of each line. If the first line has 5 claps, the second has 7 and the third has 5, you have the 5-7-5 pattern. A haiku is not the same as a limerick, which is a funny five-line poem with a different rhyme pattern.
fact: A haiku is a very short poem from Japan, usually three lines long.
fact: A haiku usually has 5 syllables in line one, 7 in line two and 5 in line three, so 17 in all.
fact: A haiku usually paints one small moment, often about nature or a season.
fact: A haiku often has a seasonal word, such as snow, blossom or leaves, and a surprise or turn at the end.
fact: «Haiku» means a very short poem with a 5-7-5 syllable pattern.
exercise: How many lines does a haiku usually have? | Five | Two | Seven | *Three
exercise: «In English schools a haiku is usually three lines of 5, 7 and 5 syllables.» How many syllables does a haiku have in all? | *17 | 5 | 20 | 12
exercise: Which line of a haiku has 7 syllables? | All three lines | The third line | The first line | *The second line
test: «Haiku are often about nature, but they can catch any small everyday moment, even at a petrol station.» What is a haiku most likely to show? | A joke with a rhyme at the end | A list of rules for a game | *One small moment, such as a leaf falling | A long story with ten characters
test: What is a haiku's usual syllable pattern for its three lines? | 7-5-7 | *5-7-5 | 3-4-3 | 10-10-10
exam: Which statement about haiku is true? | *A haiku usually has three lines of 5, 7 and 5 syllables | A haiku is always five lines long | A haiku is a long story with many characters | A haiku must rhyme in every line
